Z||000000||Loki||04-24-2001||12:23 PM||||OK I just spent the last 20 minutes not knowing what I was doing and got the front rotors off the 85 parts car..Now then to ou them on the 86 what has to be done? Simple replacement? Or anyhitng I SHOULD know   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Tigger||04-24-2001||12:32 PM||||Repack the bearings with a little more grease if possible.  Don't see why the rotors couldn't be swapped.  Check brake pad wear, re-lube the caliper slides with that high temp red colored lube.<P>Here's what I do to put the rotor back on:<P>Tighten the wheel nut down to seat the bearings (12 ft lbs).  Loosen till just finger tight then back off to next cotter key hole and put the cotter key back on.<P>That's all I can think of at the moment.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Tigger (edited 04-24-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||Loki||04-24-2001||12:40 PM||||Coolio...Gonna replace pads and calipers are good..Not used much on the 85 till it died...Also whats the best way to paint calipers? Might as well since ive got em out.<BR>Thanx''<BR><P>------------------<BR>Loki<BR>ICQ# 16477998<BR>www.cox-internet.com/fiero  !!!UPDATED!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||theogre||04-24-2001||06:52 PM||||The OE calipers are aluminum. just clean them up good and they look allot beter. Otherwise you need some kind of hightemp engine paint.||||reg||1
Z||000004||rogergarrison||04-24-2001||07:21 PM||||i just use regular automotive paint. Its lasted for years on my cars. main thing it to get them really clean. also brake fluid will take it off like stripper so be careful doing brake work after their painted. Lisa painted hers, ive painted mine too.||||reg||1
Z||000005||jch82||04-24-2001||09:25 PM||||I was always told that if you replace the pads that you have to either replace the rotors if they are shot or machine the old rotors so they are clean. Otherwise you will be buying pads again....really soon.<P>I just did the front rotors on my fiero and I machined my old rotors down, put new pads on and regreased everything...Very easy job, just have to watch out so you don't strip out the torx bolts behind the calipers...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||6
